  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hardest-to-Reach Somalia (H2R Somalia)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acumen&#x2019;s $250 million investment initiativeH2R is providing impact-linked capital and targeted technical assistance to off-grid solar companies in 16 underserved energy access markets in sub-Saharan Africa. The Hardest-to-Reach initiative leverages Acumen&#x2019;s 15-year track record in decentralised renewable energy investing to activate these most challenging geographies, which are at risk of being left behind in the global energytransition.&#xa3;2 million in grant funding from FCDO Somalia will catalyse Somalia&#x2019;s nascent energy access market. Aligned with PM Sunak&#x2019;s COP28 commitment to facilitate&#x2018;clean energy demonstrators&#x2019;, we see a unique opportunity in Somalia for Acumen to leverage its partnership with Green Climate Fund (GCF), USAID Power Africa, and the World Bank&#x2019;s ASCENT program. By working together to fuel the expansion of decentralised renewable energy companies in Somalia, FCDO, Acumen and its partners can demonstrate the viability of a commercial, competitive energy access industry built to deliver clean energy pathways out of poverty for thepeople of Somalia.</narrative>
  </description>
